      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like something that might fit into the backend-specific sub-options of `--hypervisor`, so it could be something like:\n\n```\npub enum HypervisorKind {\n    ...\n\n    Gunyah {\n        device: Option\u003cPathBuf\u003e,\n        vm_name: Option\u003cString\u003e,\n    },\n}\n```\n\nOn the command line, this would look like:\n\n```\ncrosvm run --hypervisor gunyah[device\u003d/dev/gunyah,vm-name\u003dMyName] ...\n```\n\nThis is slightly different than the existing info we have in `HypervisorKind`, but I think it would fit okay there. Keeping it as a separate option is reasonable too, although I would prefer a different, more descriptive option name than `--qualcomm-trusted-vm\u003dMyName` (if that is indeed what it is).",
